Variables and function declarations are moved to the top of their scope during compilation.

```javascript
console.log(x); // undefined (not ReferenceError)
var x = 5;

// Interpreted as:
var x;
console.log(x);
x = 5;
```

A function that has access to variables from its outer scope even after the outer function has returned.

```javascript
function outer() {
  let count = 0;
  return function inner() {
    count++;
    return count;
  }
}
const counter = outer();
counter(); // 1
counter(); // 2
```

Refers to the object that is executing the current function. Its value depends on how the function is called.

```javascript
const obj = {
  name: "John",
  greet() { console.log(this.name); }
};
obj.greet(); // "John"
```

A function passed as an argument to another function to be executed later.

```javascript
function fetchData(callback) {
  setTimeout(() => callback("data"), 1000);
}
fetchData((data) => console.log(data));
```

Using a single event listener on a parent to handle events from multiple children.

```javascript
document.querySelector('ul').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  if (e.target.tagName === 'LI') {
    console.log(e.target.textContent);
  }
});
```

Expands iterables into individual elements.

```javascript
const arr1 = [1, 2];
const arr2 = [...arr1, 3, 4]; // [1, 2, 3, 4]
const obj = { a: 1, ...{ b: 2 } }; // { a: 1, b: 2 }
```

Collects remaining arguments into an array.

```javascript
function sum(...numbers) {
  return numbers.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
}
sum(1, 2, 3, 4); // 10
```

String literals with embedded expressions using backticks.

```javascript
const name = "John";
const greeting = `Hello, ${name}!`;
```

Creates new function with `this` set to provided value.

```javascript
const obj = { name: "John" };
function greet() { console.log(this.name); }
const boundGreet = greet.bind(obj);
boundGreet(); // "John"
```

Both invoke function with specified `this`, but `apply()` takes array of arguments.

```javascript
function greet(greeting, punctuation) {
  console.log(`${greeting}, ${this.name}${punctuation}`);
}
const obj = { name: "John" };
greet.call(obj, "Hello", "!"); // "Hello, John!"
greet.apply(obj, ["Hello", "!"]); // "Hello, John!"
```

Function that always returns same output for same input and has no side effects.

```javascript
// Pure
const add = (a, b) => a + b;

// Impure
let total = 0;
const addToTotal = (x) => total += x;
```

Shorthand for if-else statement.

```javascript
const age = 18;
const canVote = age >= 18 ? "yes" : "no";
```

- Shallow: copies top level only
- Deep: copies all nested levels

```javascript
// Shallow
const obj1 = { a: 1, b: { c: 2 } };
const shallow = { ...obj1 };
shallow.b.c = 3; // affects obj1.b.c

// Deep
const deep = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj1));
```

Array-like object containing all arguments passed to a function.

```javascript
function sum() {
  return Array.from(arguments).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
}
sum(1, 2, 3); // 6
```

Creates instance of constructor function or class.

```javascript
function Person(name) {
  this.name = name;
}
const john = new Person("John");
```

Object from which other objects inherit properties and methods.

```javascript
function Person(name) {
  this.name = name;
}
Person.prototype.greet = function() {
  console.log(`Hello, ${this.name}`);
};
```

Objects inherit directly from other objects.

```javascript
const parent = { greet() { console.log("Hi"); } };
const child = Object.create(parent);
child.greet(); // "Hi"
```

Creates new object with specified prototype.

```javascript
const parent = { greet() { console.log("Hi"); } };
const child = Object.create(parent);
child.greet(); // "Hi"
```

Tests if object is instance of constructor.

```javascript
function Person() {}
const john = new Person();
john instanceof Person; // true
```

Function parameters with default values if not provided.

```javascript
function greet(name = "Guest") {
  console.log(`Hello, ${name}`);
}
greet(); // "Hello, Guest"
```
